

L4TLauncher currently ignores any key in extra_uEnv.txt other than
custom_fdt_file, so the extra_os_firmware_class_path entry written by
meta-balena's os-extra-firmware service into extra_uEnv.txt is parsed
but never appended to the kernel command line, meaning
firmware_class.path does not survive a reboot.

This backports the extra_os_firmware_class_path parsing and BootArgs
concatenation already shipped for the Orin/Thor L4TLauncher patches
(balena-jetson-orin commit 6ceaba9, 2025-12-05), and moves the
ProcessExtrauEnv() call to run unconditionally (matching upstream)
instead of only when extlinux.conf has an "FDT default" entry.

Upstream-status: Inappropriate [configuration]
Signed-off-by: guille-vega <guillermo.vega@balena.io>

Index: edk2-tegra/edk2-nvidia/Silicon/NVIDIA/Application/L4TLauncher/L4TLauncher.c
